uid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/an-english-couple-paved-a-1-4-metre-wedge-of-their-neighbours-garden-to-widen-access-to-a-horse-paddock-in-2017-a-tribunal-has-rejected-their-claim-to-the-land-leaving-the-disputed-driveway-at-risk/articleshow/135671364.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135671407,imgsize-1196400.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Iowa Supreme Court overturns foreclosure after lender failed to notify a co-owner of the default]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135678777.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a landmark decision, the Iowa Supreme Court determined that Lynae D McMillen Dickey Tesdall, a co-owner of a property, must receive notice before any foreclosure actions can proceed. Despite not signing the promissory note, she was listed as a borrower in the mortgage. While absent, missed payments accumulated, and Wells Fargo neglected to inform her of the ongoing overdue amount.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-iowa-woman-co-owned-a-house-bought-with-a-260775-mortgage-but-never-signed-the-loan-note-when-the-lender-tried-to-foreclose-without-notifying-her-the-state-supreme-court-reversed-the-foreclosure-ruling/articleshow/135678777.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-iowa-woman-co-owned-a-house-bought-with-a-260775-mortgage-but-never-signed-the-loan-note-when-the-lender-tried-to-foreclose-without-notifying-her-the-state-supreme-court-reversed-the-foreclosure-ruling/articleshow/135678777.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T04:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135679059,imgsize-1641985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Old Masters Evening Sale: rare Altdorfer oil emerges after decades; expected to fetch up to £5 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135671135.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An extraordinary Renaissance masterpiece by Albrecht Altdorfer, estimated at £3 million to £5 million, is set for auction. Having been part of a private Swiss collection since 1957, this painting promises to be a rare find. Prior to the auction, it will grace exhibits in both New York and London, showcasing Altdorfer's revolutionary landscapes that brilliantly emphasize nature's significance in art.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-renaissance-landscape-bought-by-a-swiss-collector-in-1957-vanished-from-public-view-for-nearly-70-years-experts-have-identified-it-as-a-rare-altdorfer-worth-up-to-5-million/articleshow/135671135.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-renaissance-landscape-bought-by-a-swiss-collector-in-1957-vanished-from-public-view-for-nearly-70-years-experts-have-identified-it-as-a-rare-altdorfer-worth-up-to-5-million/articleshow/135671135.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135671185,imgsize-74220.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hawaii supreme court to hear elephant habeas corpus plea over sanctuary release]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135707264.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hawaii-supreme-court-to-hear-whether-two-elephants-held-at-honolulu-zoo-for-decades-can-challenge-their-captivity-through-habeas-corpus-conservation-group-seeks-their-release-to-a-sanctuary/articleshow/135707264.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hawaii-supreme-court-to-hear-whether-two-elephants-held-at-honolulu-zoo-for-decades-can-challenge-their-captivity-through-habeas-corpus-conservation-group-seeks-their-release-to-a-sanctuary/articleshow/135707264.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T03:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135707375,imgsize-257595.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas family gets $21.6 million after faulty plumbing makes home unfit to live in]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135675893.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas family has been awarded more than $21.6 million after faulty plumbing sent sewer gas into their home, which they bought in 2018. A plumber later found that the sewer vents ended in the attic. The family reported health problems and had to leave the house, which remains uninhabitable.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-family-noticed-a-strong-smell-before-buying-their-new-home-in-2018-years-later-a-plumber-found-its-sewer-vents-ended-in-the-attic-and-a-tarrant-county-jury-has-awarded-them-more-than-21-6-million/articleshow/135675893.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-family-noticed-a-strong-smell-before-buying-their-new-home-in-2018-years-later-a-plumber-found-its-sewer-vents-ended-in-the-attic-and-a-tarrant-county-jury-has-awarded-them-more-than-21-6-million/articleshow/135675893.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T03:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135676693,imgsize-142850.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Generation Be There Campaign: Lady Gaga-backed course tops 100,000 learners; skills boost peer support]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135671016.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Lady Gaga's Born This Way Foundation, collaborating with Jack dot org, has introduced the Be There Certificate programme. This initiative empowers individuals to identify mental health issues and offer necessary support. Since its inception in March 2022, over 100,000 people have successfully completed the complimentary online course. Participants feel more confident in assisting others facing these challenges, promoting a culture of awareness and accountability in mental health welfare.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/lady-gagas-foundation-and-jack-org-set-out-to-help-people-support-friends-struggling-with-mental-health-more-than-100000-people-have-now-completed-their-be-there-certificate-training/articleshow/135671016.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/lady-gagas-foundation-and-jack-org-set-out-to-help-people-support-friends-struggling-with-mental-health-more-than-100000-people-have-now-completed-their-be-there-certificate-training/articleshow/135671016.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135671077,imgsize-803964.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sinatra's ex-wife Nancy's former Beverly Hills home rents for $27,495 a month]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135707085.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/frank-sinatras-former-wife-nancy-barbato-lived-in-this-beverly-hills-estate-for-years-the-one-acre-property-is-now-available-for-27495-a-month/articleshow/135707085.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/frank-sinatras-former-wife-nancy-barbato-lived-in-this-beverly-hills-estate-for-years-the-one-acre-property-is-now-available-for-27495-a-month/articleshow/135707085.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135707179,imgsize-162522.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Louisiana court rejects ex-wife’s claim to husband’s Raising Cane’s stake after divorce]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135672349.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Anne McQueen sought to claim business interests from her ex-husband years after their divorce settlement agreement. The Louisiana Court of Appeal upheld the prior ruling, stating property division was already settled in 2007. John's business interests, acquired before marriage, were deemed allocated to him under their consent judgment. The court emphasized that the 2007 agreement waived further claims about community property.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-man-acquired-an-early-stake-linked-to-raising-canes-before-marrying-in-2001-after-their-2007-divorce-settlement-his-former-wife-sought-a-share-of-the-interests-but-a-2026-appeals-court-rejected-her-claim/articleshow/135672349.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-man-acquired-an-early-stake-linked-to-raising-canes-before-marrying-in-2001-after-their-2007-divorce-settlement-his-former-wife-sought-a-share-of-the-interests-but-a-2026-appeals-court-rejected-her-claim/articleshow/135672349.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T02:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135672527,imgsize-1996576.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South Carolina's 229-acre White Tract to be conserved after 20-year fight against housing development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135677793.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable show of environmental cooperation, a 229-acre tract in South Carolina will transition to permanent conservation after development plans were challenged. Concerns over wetlands, wildlife, and water quality catalyzed a settlement enabling the Open Space Institute to acquire land adjacent to the Cape Romain National Wildlife Refuge. This outcome is a triumph for conservation advocates who have dedicated years to preserve this vital ecological region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2006-a-developer-planned-more-than-200-homes-on-a-229-acre-south-carolina-tract-bordering-a-wildlife-refuge-after-20-years-of-opposition-it-has-agreed-to-sell-the-land-for-permanent-conservation/articleshow/135677793.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2006-a-developer-planned-more-than-200-homes-on-a-229-acre-south-carolina-tract-bordering-a-wildlife-refuge-after-20-years-of-opposition-it-has-agreed-to-sell-the-land-for-permanent-conservation/articleshow/135677793.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-11T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135678037,imgsize-2377715.cms"/></item><item><title><